<http://data.silknow.org/object/2d6d4118-ce0c-3817-b6c2-82b236bed75e>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Silk shawl, possibly Lyon, France, ca. 1860-1870."@en , "Shawl made from woven silk with a red ground on which are narrow white stripes containing brightly coloured rosettes, eight-pointed stars and lozenges. In between are overlapping tape meanders and arabesques on a variety of patterned grounds.\nThere is a narrow border all around the shawl which has a pattern of a multiple ogival lattice containing flower-heads. At either end is a 'van dyke' pattern interrupted by a special motif at the end of each stripe.\nThe colours are wine red, intense mid-blue, dark green, yellow, pink/purple, black and white.\nThere is a simple warp fringe, the additional warp in the white stripe being knotted on top of a similarly knotted red silk fringe. Between these areas the fringe is not knotted.\nThere is a black silk selvedge and the loose silk bound on the back finishes neatly around a cord at the beginning of the selvedge."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/416d21fc-93f1-3dbb-a5d0-9f2ebe8b613b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Shawl made from woven silk with a red ground on which are narrow white stripes containing brightly coloured rosettes, eight-pointed stars and lozenges. In between are overlapping tape meanders and arabesques on a variety of patterned grounds.\nThere is a narrow border all around the shawl which has a pattern of a multiple ogival lattice containing flower-heads. At either end is a 'van dyke' pattern interrupted by a special motif at the end of each stripe.\nThe colours are wine red, intense mid-blue, dark green, yellow, pink/purple, black and white.\nThere is a simple warp fringe, the additional warp in the white stripe being knotted on top of a similarly knotted red silk fringe. Between these areas the fringe is not knotted.\nThere is a black silk selvedge and the loose silk bound on the back finishes neatly around a cord at the beginning of the selvedge."@en , "Silk shawl, possibly Lyon, France, ca. 1860-1870."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/2d6d4118-ce0c-3817-b6c2-82b236bed75e/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/2d6d4118-ce0c-3817-b6c2-82b236bed75e/dimension/2> ;
